Let X be open in R^n and f:X -> R be a scalar-valued function; let a = (a₁, a₂, ..., a(sub(n))) ∈ X. 
We say that f is differentiable at a if all the parital derivatives f(sub(x))(a), i = 1, ..., n, exist and if the function h:R^n -> R defined by 

	h(x) = f(a) + f(sub(x₁))(a) (x₁ - a₁) + f(x₂)(a) (x₂ - a₂) + ... + f(x(sub(n)))(a) (x(sub(n)) - a(sub(n)))

is a good linear approximation to f near a, meaning that 

	
	lim(x -> a) (f(x) - h(x))/(||x - a||) = 0
